  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Selected proposal, not implementation",
      "items": [
        "Existing hooks are pinned at d0c268a4. A private cycle lane and process timer are proposed; no C5 runtime check has run.",
        "Three independent sketches, two actual providers and a fresh judge informed selection. Remaining implementation gates are not waived."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Admission and clocks stay bounded",
      "items": [
        "Reuse source64/8192 pool, Attempts180s and request wait<=3s. The collector can outlive outer600s tracking, as before.",
        "Memo-driven wakeup avoids fixed-interval jitter. Local fallback never bypasses provider funding, attempts or overlap."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Stop and uncertainty",
      "items": [
        "Prebuild the running lease; never drop it inside a watch write lock. Verify provider destruction before completion is signaled.",
        "Stop guard aborts actual inner work on deadline/drop. Async cancellation is not synchronous join; incomplete drain stays Unknown. Existing5s/34s budgets and log schema remain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Publication and remaining evidence",
      "items": [
        "Source/public warning services are distinct. Keep source invalidation only; no new cache-generation or shared-memory guarantee.",
        "Silent initial baselines remain. No-HTTP feed-event smoke needs an explicit quiet durable baseline plus a new provider publication; it does not prove initial delivery.",
        "Private protocol tests, owned process CLI, current source review/CI and placement still precede pre-merge. No live calls, sends, merge, deployment or global closure."
      ]
    }
  ]
